{
  "description": "Local-mode Tasks contract between the SDKs and `keelson dev task run <name> --payload - --json` (T-1037). The CLI prints exactly one JSON object on stdout: {\"task\": {...}} when the declared command ran (succeeded or failed; the CLI exits 0 / 1), otherwise {\"error\": {...}} (the CLI's structured error; readers look only at error.code). The SDK ignores the CLI's exit code and decides from stdout alone. `task_keys` is the exact key set of the task object; the CLI test pins its real output to it. Each case's `stdout` (a JSON value, printed compactly) or `stdout_text` (raw text) is what a fake CLI prints; `sdk` is the expected SDK outcome: `status` is what get(task_id) returns afterwards (the seven production fields; exit_code and timed_out are dropped), `error_code` is the TasksError code enqueue raises/returns.",
